{"parentUuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007", "isSidechain": true, "userType": "external", "sessionId": "30f683b4-388a-4c04-89f4-612b7fe60362", "version": "2.1.0", "gitBranch": "main", "agentId": "agent-fixture-01", "type": "assistant", "uuid": "00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000008", "timestamp": "2026-09-30T10:01:56.000Z", "message": {"id": "msg_01Fixture0008", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The loader is imported by every module under the runtime package before that module reads its own configuration, which is why the ordering matters: a module that reads its configuration first sees the built-in defaults rather than the repository layer, and the two call sites that do so are the replay window and the digest writer. Moving the import above the read in both places keeps every module on the same layer, and the test that pins the order now passes on both paths."}], "stop_reason": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 40}}}
